    {
      "color": "blue",
      "data": {
        "text": "## 1. Inputs and controls\n\nSupply paired short reads and optional long reads. Metadata defines sample groups. Choose original, grouped or hybrid samples; single, multi or both coverage strategies; and Binette, DAS Tool or both refiners."
      },
      "id": 1,
      "position": [
        30,
        35
      ],
      "size": [
        380,
        260
      ],
      "type": "markdown"
    },
    {
      "color": "green",
      "data": {
        "text": "## 3. Assembly\n\nMEGAHIT assembles short reads. metaSPAdes can also use supplied long reads. Alternatively, provide custom assemblies. Their identifiers and order must match the selected samples. QUAST checks the selected assemblies."
      },
      "id": 5,
      "position": [
        1720,
        35
      ],
      "size": [
        380,
        260
      ],
      "type": "markdown"
    },
    {
      "color": "lime",
      "data": {
        "text": "## 4. Coverage strategies\n\nSingle coverage maps each selected sample\u2019s reads to its own assembly. Multi coverage maps all original read samples to every selected assembly. Choose Both to run both branches. Enabled binners use the resulting alignments and contig depths."
      },
      "id": 7,
      "position": [
        2340,
        35
      ],
      "size": [
        380,
        260
      ],
      "type": "markdown"
    },
    {
      "color": "orange",
      "data": {
        "text": "## 5. Refine and combine bins\n\nBinette and/or DAS Tool refine candidate bins in each coverage branch. Flattening removes empty skipped branches; merging combines the selected results; nesting restores sample/bin structure. Name conflicts across coverage branches receive suffixes."
      },
      "id": 9,
      "position": [
        2960,
        35
      ],
      "size": [
        820,
        260
      ],
      "type": "markdown"
    },
    {
      "color": "red",
      "data": {
        "text": "## 6. Quality and dereplication\n\nPool refined bins and assess completeness and contamination with CheckM2. Keep bins with a quality result, format the quality table for dRep, then apply the selected quality, size and ANI thresholds to choose representative MAGs."
      },
      "id": 11,
      "position": [
        4030,
        35
      ],
      "size": [
        380,
        260
      ],
      "type": "markdown"
    }
  ],
